WEBVTT

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:15.970
<i>Sarah.</i>

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:19.930
Sarah.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:30.900
Your hair's a mess.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:35.820
Monica.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.080
You push yourself too hard.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.540
Remember what I said?

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.540
If your emotions take control...

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.630
you'll lose sight of what you should do.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.470
Whenever you're lost...

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:03.560
just try stepping back.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:07.770
Okay.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:23.950
Monica?

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.680
Monica! Monica!

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.200
<i>Now for our next story.</i>

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.410
<i>The Justice Department announced</i>
<i>that they would be</i>

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.740
<i>deferring prosecution of LIVE Corporation</i>

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.290
<i>for the bribery case.</i>

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.500
<i>It appears the Justice Department</i>
<i>has partially accepted</i>

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:57.260
<i>the defense team's claims</i>
<i>that key evidence was inadmissible.</i>

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.840
<i>Chairman Martland,</i>
<i>who has been denying any wrongdoing...</i>

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.710
This is James.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.130
It's me.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.960
I looked over all the camera footage
you asked me to.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.470
What did you find?

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.970
I don't know if it's connected,

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.810
but I did find a suspicious vehicle
near the area.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:13.020
I'll be right there!

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.190
James.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.450
I found it again.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.200
Put it up.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.200
Can you link them?

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:32.450
Copy that.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.540
<i>Are they chasing something?</i>

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:42.920
<i>Or trying to get away?</i>

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.470
Eddy.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.970
How long will it take to identify the--?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:52.930
Where's Eddy?

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:56.350
-Don't know.
-Don't know.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.240
What are you doing here?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.250
Yo.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:24.590
Perfect timing.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:26.050
Look at this.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.630
We'll be able to detect
a more accurate location.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:31.550
Its signal is harder to jam as well.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:34.560
Now...

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.060
it won't matter who we face.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.770
It should've been you.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:45.320
What?

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.190
If you were there...

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.280
things would've been different.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:54.330
You would've saved Theo.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Theo just wanted to go home.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.040
And I promised him.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.100
I couldn't...

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.010
keep my promise.

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:22.810
This case...

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.230
We have to solve it.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:30.650
Right?

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:13.320
It's fine.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:17.580
Could you pour a cup of mint tea
for my friend as well?

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:39.140
Despite all the noise outside...

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.730
it's quiet in here.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.320
It's a good spot.

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:54.950
It has the best falafels.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:04.460
We conducted tests on the product
in the desert.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.920
The client was very pleased.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:10.670
And...

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.050
just as you said,
we've been approached by the military.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:19.510
As one would expect of Steven Martland.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.520
You know how to play the game.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:28.190
The Masks are just tools
used to continue this game.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.360
It's very like you.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:32.900
I can respect it.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.540
The SSC have gotten involved.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.710
I'm temporarily suspending
its development.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:50.670
The SSC?

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.300
That's right.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:04.430
Sorry, excuse me.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:09.440
It's too sweet.

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:16.280
You'll learn to appreciate it.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.820
Give it time.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.810
Mommy, hurry up!

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:52.690
Hurry up!

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.270
May!

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.230
Your hat!

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:57.900
Here.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:03.160
Look at this!

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.160
It's super pretty, isn't it?

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.000
That's...

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.380
I hope we can find a cute bottle.

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.420
Theo.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:38.860
-We can't find her!
-Try the roof.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.830
Are you an acquaintance of Sarah Sinclair?

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:54.830
Yes.

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:57.210
She's been missing since this morning.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.050
Sarah.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.100
<i>-The number you dialed cannot be--</i>
-Damn it!

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:13.480
Sarah!

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:14.940
<i>Sorry, it's me.</i>

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:19.570
I found the vehicle
from the security footage.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:20.900
That's good.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:22.400
Where is it?

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.820
I sent you the details.
Lisa's heading there now.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:27.030
Okay.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:41.550
You're right.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:43.840
We did distribute this photograph.

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:48.140
It was a small symposium.

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:50.720
Something about applied technology.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:53.730
Let's see...

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:55.560
Maybe around here?

00:12:57.230 --> 00:13:00.360
I think it's organized by year.

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:02.570
Thank you.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:08.240
Seems like you folks in prosecution
are getting buried in work recently.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:10.240
Yes, I suppose.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:14.750
I tried looking into this particular case,

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.420
but turned up nothing.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.500
Is there anything you know?

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:26.090
Thank you.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.760
I can manage on my own from here.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:29.680
Take your time.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:45.400
Just great!

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.910
I don't want it left unsolved.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.620
I figure you'd be able to understand
this feeling.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:06.510
My feelings don't matter.

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:15.220
This...

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:17.640
It's the LIVE Corporation.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.980
Fred was with LIVE.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:14.140
Are you okay?

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:16.640
James.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:18.760
You had me worried sick.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:32.400
It's a symposium for applied technology
held a few years ago.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:37.660
It was mostly attended
by genetic and cellular researchers.

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.500
This man here...

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:42.750
is Fred Faraday.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.710
Genetic engineering, neuroscience.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:49.920
He's a scientist who studies the unknown
mysteries of the human condition.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.050
Fred is the man Monica met with

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:57.760
right before her death.

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.020
And this man...

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:03.770
Wait, isn't this guy...

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:05.560
<i>What was it?</i>

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:09.020
LIVE Corporation.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:13.190
Fred worked for them.

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:14.110
LIVE.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.740
It's from Lisa about the vehicle.

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:21.450
Yeah. She didn't find anything.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:24.790
-Vehicle?
-We found a suspicious vehicle

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:28.040
from that night not far from the incident.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.050
We haven't ID'd an owner yet.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:34.420
That's Fred's.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.680
It's the car Monica was in.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:39.010
I'm positive!

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.350
He's the key to this case!

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:43.680
Where is it? Do you know?

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:48.020
They fished it out of the river today.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.190
What do you mean?

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:54.940
Are you saying Fred is...?

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:59.240
No.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:05.660
Not much has been brought to the surface,

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:08.370
but LIVE is an unethical company.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:13.300
If Fred was meeting with Monica,
a prosecutor...

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:16.090
then it's likely...

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:18.470
he was a whistleblower.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:23.850
Then maybe the pictures of the Mask
were from him.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:30.400
Sarah!

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.690
-What are you doing?
-What do you mean?

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:38.030
I'm going to pay LIVE a visit right now,
obviously!

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:40.530
-You can't.
-Why not?

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:41.740
Sarah!

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:46.250
This is as far as you go.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.000
What?

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:51.750
I want you...

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.340
to leave the rest to us, to the SSC.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:58.380
What?

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:00.930
You can't do this to me!

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:05.010
-Monica's case is my case!
-Sarah!

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:08.020
You can't take me off now!

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:12.100
James!

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:18.440
I'm used to most dangers.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:22.280
But this is different.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:26.870
I can't let this case
get anyone else killed.

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:31.500
So...

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.630
you're saying I'm in the way.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:39.380
That's right.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:45.970
Sarah.

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:50.390
Do you have a second?

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:20.840
Evidently, the face was already carved off
by the time it was found.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:25.010
Apparently, people project their lives...

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:29.770
onto this statue by the unknown artist.

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:32.980
And what do you see...

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:35.440
when you look at this statue?

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:42.990
Personally,

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:46.990
I think the artist
carved the face off himself.

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:52.290
He wanted to transform into someone else.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:53.910
No.

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:56.420
He created this statue
as a rite of passage

00:20:56.500 --> 00:21:00.090
in order to change and do something.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:03.170
Then...

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.010
he carved the face off.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:11.770
Mystery stimulates the imagination.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:14.390
What do you see...

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:18.860
in this statue?

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:27.990
I'm temporarily suspending
all Mask development.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.580
Connor won't be happy.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.750
I want him brought in...

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:40.340
before he does something foolish.

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:50.890
That shouldn't be a problem.

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:54.390
You know...

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:56.640
I love my job.

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:00.730
I want to do it as long as possible.

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:43.610
Just as I thought.

00:22:46.070 --> 00:22:47.570
He's still alive.

00:24:19.410 --> 00:24:21.910
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
